pySMESH: a size given to a face goes to that face (NETGENPlugin V9_16_0; applies after
NETGENPlugin_edge_local_size_ends.patch).

Defect: with NETGEN_V6 defined, NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx sets a face's maximal size with
occgeo.SetFaceMaxH(faceNgID-1, val, netgen::mparam) for a local size on a face
(SetLocalSize), and with occgeo.SetFaceMaxH(i-1, size, netgen::mparam) for the chordal
error of a cylinder, sphere or torus face (SetLocalSizeForChordalError). faceNgID and i are
1-based indices into occgeo.fmap. In netgen 6.2.2101 the overload
SetFaceMaxH(int facenr, double faceh, const MeshingParameters&) also takes a 1-based face
number (libsrc/occ/occgeom.hpp:353-372: face_maxh[facenr-1], and nothing for facenr < 1);
only SetFaceMaxH(size_t facenr, double faceh) is 0-based. So the size went to the face
before, and face 1's size went nowhere. Measured on a 4 x 4 x 4 cube at max_size 1.0 with
a local size of 0.1 on one face: the parallel face 4 away is refined to a mean triangle edge
of 0.114 to 0.116, and a chordal error of 0.002 on a cylinder of radius 1 left its lateral
face at a mean edge of 0.41 (tests/test_mesher_netgen_face_size.py).

Change, in NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx only: both calls pass the 1-based index. A mesh with no
local size on a face and no chordal error does not change.

diff --git a/src/NETGENPlugin/NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx b/src/NETGENPlugin/NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx
--- a/src/NETGENPlugin/NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx
+++ b/src/NETGENPlugin/NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx
@@ -816,7 +816,9 @@
     if ( faceNgID >= 1 )
     {
 #ifdef NETGEN_V6
-      occgeo.SetFaceMaxH(faceNgID-1, val, netgen::mparam);
+      // pySMESH: this overload takes the 1-based face number (occgeom.hpp), as fmap does;
+      // faceNgID-1 gave the size to the face before, and none for face 1.
+      occgeo.SetFaceMaxH(faceNgID, val, netgen::mparam);
 #else
       occgeo.SetFaceMaxH(faceNgID, val);
 #endif
@@ -885,7 +887,8 @@
       double maxCurv = Max( Abs( surfProp.MaxCurvature()), Abs( surfProp.MinCurvature() ));
       double    size = elemSizeForChordalError( _chordalError, 1 / maxCurv );
 #ifdef NETGEN_V6
-      occgeo.SetFaceMaxH( i-1, size * sizeCoef, netgen::mparam );
+      // pySMESH: 1-based, as above.
+      occgeo.SetFaceMaxH( i, size * sizeCoef, netgen::mparam );
 #else
       occgeo.SetFaceMaxH( i, size * sizeCoef );
 #endif
